Chapter 5: Broken Things
首次登场
Chapter 5 Cinematic Trailer: Welcome Home (reveal)
Chapter 5: Broken Things (physically)

She is a little asking Annie! Ooooh, please take me out of my case. Oooooh, please rescue the orphans. Oooh, please blow up the whole factory. And BURN. EVERYONE. ALIVE!!!

Lily Lovebraids mocking Poppy Playtime, Chapter 5: Broken Things
莉莉·爱辫儿 is a toy produced by Playtime Co. She appeared as a secondary antagonist in Chapter 5: Broken Things.

In 1995, Playtime's scientists used her likeness to create Experiment 1468. Although her design and controllable hair had been finalized by August 6, they had not chosen a candidate at that time. Two days later, the toys turned on the company staff and slaughtered them. One employee was taken prisoner: Gracie Green, a high-ranking counselor who had psychologically tortured the experiments to embrace their new identities. For her transgressions, Gracie was elected as Experiment 1468's candidate, surgically transformed, and subjected to her own conditioning. Her identity and crimes forgotten, Lily was sentenced to isolation by The Prototype and exiled to Sweet Street in 1996. Lily took up residence in Sweet Street's dollhouse, where she continuously attempted to gain The Prototype's favor until the eventual return of The Player in 2005.

First teased in Halloween artwork by Amber Ogden, Lily was officially revealed in a cinematic trailer, which coincided with the launch of a Lily-based T-shirt that emerged from a collaboration. Her full design was showcased in the Chapter 5 Official Game Trailer.


