外貌
Lily Lovebraids is a tan ball-jointed doll that lacks a nose, has large oval-shaped eyes with black irises, round ears and blushed cheeks, and a smiling mouth framed by white teeth. She has a long curved eyelash for each eyelid. Her most notable feature is her long vibrant purple hair, which first appears wrapped into a large chignon-like style and then unfolds into three lengthy braids, with a singular bang hanging out from her forehead. She wears a purple short-sleeved t-shirt and black suspenders with a yellow star embroidered on the front pocket. Her suspenders flow out into a black triangular skirt with white diamond-shaped lining. Lily also wears purple Mary Jane shoes and black over-the-calf socks with white trims; a yellow star is embroidered on each one. While the sock on her left leg is fully extended, the one on her right leg is pulled up to her mid-calf.

In dark areas, part of Lily’s hair glows a bright purple while her eyes and teeth glow green.

When losing her temper, Lily's eyes become dilated and slightly bloodshot, exuding a manic vibe. Each of her braids also seem to end in three gnarled claws.

性格
Lily is highly energetic and possesses childlike mannerisms that border on insanity, similarly to Mommy Long Legs. She displays a fondness (or at the very least, a willingness) for tea parties, sitting down and talking to the toys she has brought there, though it is unknown if they are alive or not, excluding the Candy Cat head she whispers into. She also believes everyone she sees is a toy, including The Player. As a result of her conditioning (which involved wiping her memory) and the isolationism forced upon her by The Prototype, Lily is unable to understand why she is an outcast among The Prototype's followers. As a result of this, she is desperate for The Prototype's approval, doing anything she can to earn a place at his side as well as worrying over anything that might displease him. She also seems to harbor some level of hatred for Poppy Playtime, demanding she stopped singing while captive, displaying bitterness at Poppy being The Prototype's "favorite" despite her continued rebellions and even attempting to inflict further harm after he crushed Poppy's face. She is easily angered and tries to kill The Player for escaping.

历史
背景故事
When Playtime Co. was still active, they created and launched the Lily Lovebraids doll, in which children could braid her hair, play dress up, and have tea parties.

Lily Lovebraids was proposed by Playtime Co. as part of the Bigger Bodies Initiative, designating her as "Experiment 1468". She was designed with the ability to control her hair like a set of extra limbs. The scientists tried several attempts to get this design right before landing on a combination of horse hair, grafted finger bones, artificial bones, and other "biological materials."[3]

Gracie Green
Little did anyone expect, the subject of this experiment ended up being the lead counselor in the Wellness & Integration sector, Gracie Green, who was taken during the Hour of Joy by KickinChicken, Hoppy Hopscotch and Baba Chops in an act of vengeance for her role in the brainwashing of the other experiments.[4] After being successfully experimented on by The Prototype, she was isolated and subjected to the same conditioning treatment that she subjected other children to within the Bigger Bodies Initiative. Despite her resistance, Gracie's sanity started to deteriorate as she began forgetting her old identity and no longer recognized "Miss Gracie" as herself in the brainwashing videos. After 122 days, Gracie's mind eventually snapped and caused it to fracture into two personas: one would become her new main identity as Lily Lovebraids and another (more macabre) persona she used as an imaginary friend that was the head of a Candy Cat doll.[5] After being transferred to her toy body, the remains of Gracie lay in her bed, rotting there as a shell of whom she once was.

Eventually, she would align with The Prototype only for him to punish her further for her past crimes by relocating her into a large dollhouse that was within the Labs along Sweet Street. Lily would spend years roaming Sweet Street, driven mad by her isolation, failing to understand why she was a designated outcast as well as The Prototype rationing her food and water to the bare minimum.[6] During one of her outbursts, she smashed a window in the Dollhouse, only to cover it with her favorite poster in fear it would displease The Prototype.[7]

Chapter 5: Broken Things
In 2005, after Poppy fled through the ventilation system out of fear that The Prototype would imprison her again, she fell during her escape and was found by Lily, who captured her, locked her in the basement of her dollhouse, and intended to deliver her to The Prototype during a “tea party.” Later, Kissy Missy was captured as well while attempting to search for Poppy. She was presumably taken to become another "guest" at the party, knowing that The Prototype would most likely kill her during the meeting.

File:Lilylovebraids scene1 .jpg
Lily excitedly wraps her hair around The Player, taking them to her dollhouse.

Lily is first seen in person at the end of Sweet Street, when The Player attempts to pass through the final gates on foot. Lily appears directly behind The Player, holding a cat head, "Candy", which she uses as a puppet. Initially, she talks to The Player about inviting them to her tea party. She then unravels her hair and begins wrapping it around The Player, shouting with excitement that they will have a lot of fun.

After untangling her hair, The Player now finds themselves in Lily's dollhouse, where they have to help Lily organize her tea party, finding her guests and companions, since they are soon going to receive a "special guest". After gathering the guests (three inanimate toys), Lily returns from the kitchen and asks The Player to help with the final preparations. While Lily tidies up the kitchen, she instructs The Player to take her recipe book upstairs. When The Player goes there, they find Lily's room and, upon opening her bed, discover a skeleton lying there with an ID tag; her original body when she was still Gracie Green. Opening a dresser, they find the key to Poppy and Kissy's cell.

File:LilyTalksToGracie.png
Lily comforting Gracie Green's skeletal remains in her bed.

Lily begins to suspect someone is snooping around her room and goes to check, but The Player manages to hide in a side room in time. When Lily enters, she speaks to the lifeless skeleton (her human remains), telling it to "go back to sleep" and that "nobody’s going to hurt [it] anymore." She starts to suspect someone was there, and when she finds out who it was, she will send them to the "bad toy box."

When The Player returns to Poppy and Kissy, just as The Player is about to free them, they hear Lily approaching, forcing The Player to hide inside a vent. Lily asks what is going on, then leaves, suspecting they are trying to escape somehow. After freeing Poppy and Kissy, before they can escape, Lily grabs The Player from behind and offers them a game: when Lily hums a song, The Player can move, and when she stops, they must stay put. If they manage to reach the attic by following a purple trail using their blacklight, they win. As The Player progresses, Lily will hum faster, giving The Player less time to move.

After arriving at the Attic and reuniting with Poppy and Kissy, Lily surprises The Player again by entangling them in her hair and wrapping them up once more. When they regained consciousness, they saw that everyone is now tied together by hair around the central table. Lily begins to feel anxious and restless, as the "special guest" is about to arrive. While they wait, she begins to bother Poppy, calling her "the special guest's favorite" and starts to mock her goals and concerns, from the moment she came out of her case to her wanting to destroy the entire factory to end the lives of all the bloodthirsty toys.

File:The Tea Party.png
Lily watches in excitement as The Prototype confronts Poppy and Kissy.

Upon hearing a tremor, Lily excitedly announces the arrival of the “special guest,” laughing maniacally. As The Prototype approaches the gathering, she raises her arms and shouts “Surprise!” with childish enthusiasm. When Poppy demands to know where the orphans are, Lily mocks her ignorance. In response, The Prototype severs the head of her Candy Cat puppet in order to silence her, and Lily becomes visibly upset, crossing her arms in an exaggerated, childlike display of anger before stepping aside. She later attempts to further harm Poppy using her hair, but is struck by The Prototype, inadvertently freeing Kissy in the process.

After successfully repelling The Prototype, Kissy and The Player escape, with Kissy carrying Poppy in her only arm. As they try to escape, Lily suddenly appears through a door and desperately chases The Player throughout the Mansion, And then Lily blames them and she screaming that it is all their fault and that she will put them in the "bad toy box." Reaching the roof, The Player uses cloud-like platforms to escape, and upon reaching a maintenance exit, Lily corners them, yelling that she has done so much for them and is furious at how they repaid her.

File:Lily’s Death.gif
Lily falls from the platform, followed by the platform itself, crushing and killing her.

The Player takes advantage of Lily's rage attack to use their Pressurized Hand to detach the platform she is standing on from the ceiling, causing her to slip and try to grab onto something to prevent herself from falling, but one of her braids hits and snaps the cable holding the platform, then she falls onto the floor of the room from a great height, then the platform detaches completely, falling on her, crushing and killing her.

Abilities and Anatomy
Lily's abilities are largely tied to her long hair, which can move at will and stretch for long distances. As her name suggests, her hair is braided, giving them the appearance of sharp scorpion tails. But instead of stingers, each braid ends in a three-fingered "claw" of hair with which she can grab objects. Moreover, her hair grants her notable strength and agility, allowing her to restrain strong Bigger Body experiments like Kissy Missy, pick up fully grown adults off the ground, destroy steel walkways, and traverse the underground labs with ease. Furthermore, her hair glows purple under UV light and her eyes and teeth glow green in the dark.

你知道吗？
Lily’s various fashion options, as seen in various cutouts, indicate that she is inspired by fashion dolls like Barbie and Bratz.
In the files, theres a higher poly model for her labelled "Minnie Megabraids", this is likely to be an old name.
A cardboard cutout right after her death of her saying "Did you know your hair keeps growing even after you die?" could potentially foreshadow her return.
This "fact" is actually a misconception. After death, your hair follicles quickly die from lack of oxygen, whilst dehydration pulls the skin tight, exposing more of the hair shaft and gives the illusion that the hair is longer.
The theory that Lily could return is strengthened by the fact that Huggy Wuggy and The Doctor, both initially believed to be dead, return alive in Chapter 5.
After Lily's death scene, while her body is fully crushed under the cloud platform, her three braids remain exposed. So while Lily herself may not return alive, her implicitly still-growing hair could possibly return by itself in some way - likely to be assimilated by the Prototype as other antagonists have been.
Her design may be based on a Mommy Long Legs concept design.
There are many similarities between Lily and Mommy Long Legs.
Both are arachnid-like in their behavior. While Mommy Long Legs is obviously a spider, Lily's is more akin to a scorpion, both in the shape of her braids resembling a large stinger and a pair of claws, and how her hair glows under UV light like a scorpion's exoskeleton.
Her ability to extend her braid is reminiscent of Mommy Long Legs' ability to stretch her limbs.
It also invokes Cartoon CatNap's ability to extend his tail, as seen in his concept art.
Lily is the second character, after Mommy Long Legs, to have their name revealed via merchandise.
Both Lily and Mommy are the only characters who can change the appearance of their eyes, Mommy by dilating her pupils, Lily by constricting them.
Both are female humanoid experiments and major antagonists in their respective debut chapters.
Both are dangerously insane individuals obsessed with forcing The Player into playing games in order to kill them.
However, while Mommy's actions were partly out of revenge against a former worker at Playtime Co. for what was done to her and the children she cared for (stating that she remembers them working there), Lily is completely detached from reality and has no memory of her former life, playing her game of Redlight/Greenlight-Tag mostly just for fun and to sate her crippling loneliness.
Lily is the latest known experiment to be made prior to the Hour of Joy, with her being proposed three days prior to the event.
Lily is the second Bigger-Body monster to resemble a human being.
Lily is the third character to be named after a plant, the others being Poppy Playtime and Daisy.
In the Poppy Playtime Yule Log, Lily is presumed to be talking to Poppy.
In that same video, Lily is presumed to be singing Poppy's Lullaby. This is probably not true, however, as that theme was made for Poppy, so it is most likely Poppy herself singing it.
However, in Chapter 5, Lily is actually heard humming Poppy's Lullaby so this theory might have been true.
Her voice actress, Nicole Tompkins, is well known for playing Jill Valentine and Daniela Dimitrescu in the Resident Evil series.
Her human identity is confirmed to have been Miss Gracie, as when The Player enters her bedroom, they can find a ID card of Gracie Green. In addition, there is a voice tape that has Miss Gracie talking to herself, resembling Lily.
Lily can be heard saying certain phrases like “bad toy” and “someone who’s going in the box”, which also link her to Gracie Green.
Lily is often seen to be carrying around a broken Candy Cat head that she has conversations with, which she has named "Candy".
Lily speaks through Candy as her “aggressive” or “unhinged” side, while Lily herself represents her “kind” side.
Lily is the first character to be able to glow in the dark (her eyes and teeth at least).
During her jumpscare, the two braids that supposedly strangle the player right before the biggest one stabs the players face, forms a heart shape around Lilys neck.
There’s a segment where you have to play a Redlight Greenlight game with Lily which is similar to Statues in Chapter 2: Fly in a Web.
Lily is the third character to have more than one cardboard cutout (the first one is Huggy and the second being Mommy Long Legs).
Lily also has the most cutouts of any character in Poppy Playtime.
Lily's cutouts are the only ones in the game to have only one line of dialogue (besides her tea party themed outfit cutout which has two).
Lily is the only antagonist whose cutout does not have static.
Unlike previous bosses, Lily does not have a jingle or commercial to coincide with her toy in the game, with the commercial in her chapter being devoted to the Wrongside Outimals instead.
However, whether Lily will get a jingle or not in the future is unknown.
The background music from Lily's house is similar to "Sleep Well" by CG5.
Lily appears to have known that The Prototype had (presumably) murdered the orphans, hence why she mocked Poppy when the latter demanded to know what he did to the orphans.
One of her voice lines during her game in the dark, the line "Red Light" might be referenced to the Squid Game Doll.
Lily’s Red Light, Green Light game is similar to PJ Pug-a-Pillar’s game in Chapter 2, Statues, as they both involve not moving when music is being played or not.
Its unknown how Lily knew about the deaths of Mommy Long Legs and Doey as she mentions them being dead throughout the player getting ready for the tea party in the chapter
According to IsacX, when he left the team, Lily had some early concept art. Specifically, it showed her having two braids that she walked with, to which he compares it to Doctor Octopus from Spider-Man.[8]
However, she was not in the outline of the chapter he left, as he did not think she would fit in the chapter. Giblet, the Wrongside Outimals and Chum Chompkins were completely brand new.[8]
Lily's portrait in the attic of her dollhouse is a reference to the famous Mona Lisa painting by the Italian artist Leonardo da Vinci.
